ClusterBox structure of the MoCI pages (three menu entries: CLUSTER,
NETWORK, SYSTEM; every setting in one place):

- Login page and header say CLUSTERBOX; under the login form the
  firmware version links to its GitHub release (/moci/firmware.json,
  written at boot, readable without a session). Page title ClusterBox.
- No BMC dashboard and ADD-ONS entries in the menu (the dashboard
  repeated the cluster page; the only add-on is the ClusterBox UI).
  Reboot / restart network / restart firewall move to SYSTEM > GENERAL.
- NETWORK: no WIRELESS (the BMC has no radio), DDNS and QOS (packages
  not in the firmware); DNS & HOSTS joins DHCP ("DHCP & DNS"); tab order
  interfaces, firewall, DHCP & DNS, routes, devices, WireGuard,
  diagnostics; the first tab is the default; add-on tabs may go before a
  tab.
- SYSTEM: ADMINISTRATION is ACCESS; no LED tab (no LEDs under OpenWrt's
  control); SOFTWARE is left to the add-on (apk; the opkg status file
  does not exist on 25.12); BACKUP shows its progress; STARTUP reads
  procd's rc object (enabled at boot, running) and can enable/disable.
- Extension point "tab:section": add-ons put sections into a tab of
  the network and system pages.
- ACL: rc list and rc init.
